From 713f173890e5555f80a3fa061a4a750c344beefa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] LV11: content notes and the dark-level presentation

The nine dark levels get their content notes (plan 6.3): the card's note page
on a first visit (A goes on, B goes back; a demo skips it), the note as one
line above the goal on later visits, a moon badge and a note strip on the
level select, the first-visit bits in the BRCH arc's spare bytes (chunk size
unchanged), and the two options (Content notes: Every time / First time only;
Memorial names: On / Off), with lv_memorial_label() for the Vault.

No dark level has a map yet, so nothing shows on a real run; the host tests
re-point a level to play it. GBA RAM sections unchanged. PS1 has neither
option id and no new code: the EXE is byte-identical to the base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cz7PBDFwYoagK8oCML
